# SEO data for content with public detail pages

Any content type with a public detail page (post, project, service, product, landing page) persists a full SEO field set so admins tune it without code. Filter-only types (tags) are exempt unless they get their own URL.

## Model

- One polymorphic `SeoMeta` model (`morphTo seoable`), localized per row: `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `canonical_url`, `og_title`, `og_description`, `og_image`, `twitter_card`, `schema` (JSON-LD overrides). No per-table `meta_*` columns or parallel systems.
- The owning model has `seoMeta()` (`morphOne`) and a unique, URL-safe `slug` (`admin/slugs.mdc`).
- Public detail APIs eager-load `seoMeta` (`null` when none saved) and expose a stable lowercase `type` discriminator.
- One authorized save endpoint (e.g. `PUT /<version>/seo/{type}/{id}`) with a Form Request; URLs must be `http(s)` or same-site paths.
- SEO rows and default descriptions never fall back to another language.

## Admin fields

- SEO fields are normal form fields in an **SEO & Sharing** section on the content type's create and edit screens — never inside page/theme/form builders.
- Live counters for title (≤ 60) and description (≤ 160); `og_image` through the media picker; `twitter_card` defaults to `summary_large_image`.
- On create, save SEO after the record exists; if that call fails, keep the record and warn on the edit screen.

## Defaults cascade

Item SEO → content fields (title, excerpt, featured image) → per-type defaults → global defaults (Settings → SEO) → built-in. Resolve in one shared helper (with the title template) used by every public head.

## Adding a new SEO type

Register it in the backend type list, the frontend defaults types, and the Settings → SEO labels (all UI languages); pass its type key to the detail head helper; add it to the sitemap (`public-site/seo-head.mdc`).
